# Normalise line endings so Windows checkouts stop warning about CRLF.
# KiCad files are text, which is what makes their diffs readable.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Fabrication output is generated and must match what went to the fab
# byte for byte.
#
# The pattern is **/fab/** and not fab/**: a pattern containing a slash is
# anchored to the directory holding this file, so fab/** matched only a
# top-level fab/, and every board's outputs live one level down in
# <board>/fab/. It went unnoticed until canfuel/fab/ was first generated and
# git announced it was about to rewrite the gerbers' line endings.
**/fab/** -text
*.gbr -text
*.drl -text

# Binary, never touch.
*.pdf binary
*.step binary
*.stp binary
